                                 *********************************************

                                    NUMERICAL ELECTROMAGNETICS CODE (NEC-2D)

                                 *********************************************




                                     - - - - COMMENTS - - - -


                          Dipole with coaxial feedline.                                              
                                                                                                     
                          This file shows how you how you can model a coaxial feed                   
                          To do so, use the default Nec TL card to model the feed                    
                          and in parallel with this feed, model a wire with the                      
                          same physical length as the feedline. The length specified                 
                          in the TL card equals the physical lenght / the velocity                   
                          factor for the coax. Use 'Currents->Magnitude' on the                      
                          'Geometry (F3)' window and use Page-up/down to magnify the                 
                          current on the 'outer' of the coax. Click on the wire                      
                          resembling the Coax to see how large the current is for                    
                          the specified power input. Although the coax is fully                      
                          symmetrical with respect to the antenna the current on                     
                          the outer wire can cause trouble with RFI if the feedline                  
                          is very close to a TV/telephone-line or electrical house                   
                          wiring.                                                                    




